The saleswoman shows me a kurti.
It is a yellow kurti.
It is good cotton.
I touch the cloth.
The cloth is very soft.
I ask the price.
"What is the price of this kurti?" I ask.
"The price is six hundred rupees," the saleswoman says.
I take that yellow kurti.
I walk to the fitting room.
I put on the kurti.
I look in the mirror.
It is a good fit.
It is not a big kurti.
It is not a small kurti.
The kurti is very beautiful.
I like this yellow kurti.
I go back to the saleswoman.
"I am buying this," I say.
